    {
      "id": "bounded-linear-mapping-definition",
      "type": "definition",
      "regions": [
        [
          204,
          80,
          430,
          955,
          515
        ]
      ],
      "en": "Let $X,Y$ be normed vector spaces. A linear mapping $L:X\\to Y$ is called \\textbf{bounded} if there is a constant $C$ such that $\\|Lx\\|\\leq C\\|x\\|$ for every $x\\in X$.",
      "zh": "设 $X,Y$ 为赋范向量空间. 若存在常数 $C$, 使对每个 $x\\in X$ 有 $\\|Lx\\|\\leq C\\|x\\|$, 则称线性映射 $L:X\\to Y$ \\textbf{有界}.",
      "label": "def:bounded-linear-mapping",
      "render_role": "definition",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 204,
          "printed_page": 194,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            171.91307643714464,
            381.7677811550152,
            205.8958938723942
          ],
          "bbox_precision": "visually selected parent block, top-left PDF points",
          "crop": "workspace/crops/chapter-06-batch-15/bounded-linear-mapping-definition-204.png",
          "raw_ocr": "workspace/raw-text/pdf-0204.txt"
        }
      ],
