    {
      "id": "operator-space-norm-motivation",
      "type": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "regions": [
        [
          204,
          80,
          1350,
          955,
          1505
        ]
      ],
      "en": "It is natural to consider the set of all bounded linear mappings. It follows immediately from the definition that this set forms a vector space. Also, if we take the smallest possible constant in Definition~\\ref{def:bounded-linear-mapping}, then this quantity gives us a measure of the ``size'' of a linear mapping. This motivates the following definition.",
      "zh": "自然可以考察所有有界线性映射的集合. 由定义立即可知, 这一集合构成向量空间. 此外, 若取 Definition~\\ref{def:bounded-linear-mapping} 中可能的最小常数, 那么这个量就给出线性映射 ``大小'' 的一个度量. 这引出以下定义.",
      "label": null,
      "render_role": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 204,
          "printed_page": 194,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            539.7271004421983,
            381.7677811550152,
            601.6957675300063
          ],
          "bbox_precision": "visually selected parent block, top-left PDF points",
          "crop": "workspace/crops/chapter-06-batch-15/operator-space-norm-motivation-204.png",
          "raw_ocr": "workspace/raw-text/pdf-0204.txt"
        }
      ],
      "formula_ids": [],
      "source_review": "agent-reviewed",
      "confidence": "high",
      "cross_reference_integration": "pending full target availability"
    },
    {
      "id": "bounded-operator-space-norm-definition",
      "type": "definition",
      "regions": [
        [
          205,
          80,
          145,
          955,
          335
        ]
      ],
      "en": "By $\\mathcal{L}(X,Y)$ we denote the set of all bounded linear mappings from $X$ to $Y$. If $X=Y$, we also write $\\mathcal{L}(X)$ for $\\mathcal{L}(X,X)$. Moreover, if $L\\in\\mathcal{L}(X,Y)$, we set\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:bounded-linear-map-operator-norm}\n\\|L\\|:=\\sup_{\\|x\\|=1}\\dfrac{\\|Lx\\|}{\\|x\\|}=\\sup_{\\|x\\|\\ne0}\\dfrac{\\|Lx\\|}{\\|x\\|}.\n\\end{equation}\n",
      "zh": "用 $\\mathcal{L}(X,Y)$ 表示从 $X$ 到 $Y$ 的所有有界线性映射的集合. 若 $X=Y$, 也将 $\\mathcal{L}(X,X)$ 写为 $\\mathcal{L}(X)$. 此外, 若 $L\\in\\mathcal{L}(X,Y)$, 令\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:bounded-linear-map-operator-norm}\n\\|L\\|:=\\sup_{\\|x\\|=1}\\dfrac{\\|Lx\\|}{\\|x\\|}=\\sup_{\\|x\\|\\ne0}\\dfrac{\\|Lx\\|}{\\|x\\|}.\n\\end{equation}\n",
      "label": "def:bounded-operator-space-norm",
      "render_role": "definition",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 205,
          "printed_page": 195,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            57.9706885660139,
            381.7677811550152,
            133.93228048010107
          ],
          "bbox_precision": "visually selected parent block, top-left PDF points",
          "crop": "workspace/crops/chapter-06-batch-15/bounded-operator-space-norm-definition-205.png",
          "raw_ocr": "workspace/raw-text/pdf-0205.txt"
        }
      ],
      "formula_ids": [
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:001",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:002",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:003",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:004",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:005",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:006",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:007",
        "math:bounded-operator-space-norm-definition:008"
      ],
      "source_review": "agent-reviewed",
      "confidence": "high",
      "cross_reference_integration": "pending full target availability"
    },
    {
      "id": "bounded-operator-space-banach-theorem",
      "type": "theorem",
      "regions": [
        [
          205,
          80,
          350,
          955,
          415
        ]
      ],
      "en": "Let $X,Y$ be Banach spaces. Then $\\mathcal{L}(X,Y)$, with the norm defined by \\eqref{eq:bounded-linear-map-operator-norm}, is also a Banach space.",
      "zh": "设 $X,Y$ 为 Banach 空间. 那么 $\\mathcal{L}(X,Y)$ 在 \\eqref{eq:bounded-linear-map-operator-norm} 定义的范数下也是 Banach 空间.",
      "label": "thm:bounded-operator-space-completeness",
      "render_role": "theorem",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 205,
          "printed_page": 195,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            139.92924826279219,
            381.7677811550152,
            165.91610865445355
          ],
          "bbox_precision": "visually selected parent block, top-left PDF points",
